8. **The capability statement and the stated limits** (`docs/capabilities.md`):
   - line 168 states the graph read in parts;
   - lines 384-386 state the narrower coverage limit;
   - lines 408-409 drop «`press` holds no Ctrl …» and state `--ctrl` as ⌘ on macOS;
   - the «Where each claim is proven» section names the new tests.
   `.github/scripts/test_capability_statement.py` moves only where a count it holds moves (no verb, cause, session
   error, node key or exit status is added).

- Spec anchors:
  - `(architecture · contract/driver-verbs/press)`, `(architecture · contract/graph-verb/unpaged)`,
    `(architecture · contract/handler-coverage/bubbling)`;
  - `(architecture · decision/platform-action-modifier)`, `(architecture · decision/large-screen-in-parts)`,
    `(architecture · contract/snapshot-verb/part)`, `(architecture · decision/answers-written-by-own-json-writer)`;
  - `(architecture · decision/reached-record-before-dispatch)`, `(architecture · decision/dioxus-event-path-records-opt-in)`;
  - `(security-plan · decision/graph-answer-unpaged)`, `(security-plan · decision/boundary-widening-rule)`,
    `(security-plan · decision/closed-driver-verb-schema)`;
  - `(test-plan · contract/handler-coverage-limits/bubbling-dispatch)`, `(test-plan · decision/snapshot-text-budget)`,
    `(test-plan · decision/doc-leg-gates-public-doc-edits)`;
  - `(obs-plan · contract/command-span/snapshot-part)`, `(obs-plan · contract/graph-answer/shape)`.

- **Coverage of new surfaces:**
  - `press` argument `ctrl` → validation {schema `ArgKind::Flag`, wrong kind / repeat refused `malformed`✓} · instrumentation {command span `verb` only✓} · PII {n/a — a closed flag} · tests {unit + integ (in process, MCP, binary, kept check)} · a11y {n/a — no engine keyboard path changed; the engine's existing Ctrl/Meta arms} · tokens {n/a}
  - `graph` argument `part` → validation {`ArgKind::Part` 1–1000, 0 / 1001 / text refused `malformed`✓} · instrumentation {span records `verb` alone, no part or count✓} · PII {n/a — ids, closed words, numbers as before} · tests {unit + integ (in process, MCP, binary, kept check)} · a11y {n/a} · tokens {n/a}
  - `Outcome::GraphPart` answer → validation {n/a — output} · instrumentation {n/a} · PII {no control value or typed text✓ — the graph writer unchanged} · tests {unit `json_tests`, integ `stand_graph`} · a11y n/a · tokens n/a
